From bd140e8c40c4a78355da5902b471e8c7144c8d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:29:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09070/11362] exp6260: the focused goal prompt trades
 constant-False for constant-True; lint honesty note

RESULT. 0 of 4 non-degenerate predicates. The verdict says gate MET because one
predicate finally fired on a real win -- but that same predicate has specificity
0.0 and fires on the opening board too. The model wrote "the win condition is the
complete removal of color 42", which is true of the start grid. That is the
opposite degeneracy, not a win. dc22 is the same shape without even firing on the
win. My gate required only a sensitivity GAIN and never consulted the paired
specificity, which was sitting in the same artifact -- the third time this session
one of my own gates was too permissive.

Per the pre-registration, prompt-level work on the goal predicate is EXHAUSTED.
Framing (6255/6256), filtering (6258/6259) and focus-plus-evidence (6260) have all
been tried. What remains is non-prompt: a different representation of the win
condition, or a non-LLM inducer that generalises beyond exp4020's
structured-state single game.

LINT HONESTY NOTE. Building verdict_row_consistency_lint took five rounds, each a
real gap found by testing against real artifacts: it scanned only top-level keys
and missed its own founding case; excluded any field containing "_n" and discarded
exp6251's headline metric; printed "OK" while skipping 57 of 60 artifacts; its
paired-collapse check could not see booleans; and coercing booleans then made
NO_HEADROOM fire on every flag field. One patch used s.replace() with no assert,
silently did nothing, and cost an extra round.

It catches its three founding cases. PAIRED_METRIC_COLLAPSE now fires on exp6260
but emits five findings where one is informative, and points at the honest arm
rather than the degenerate one. Poor signal; a hint, not a verdict.

The conclusion: generic verdict-vs-rows detection over free-form artifacts needs
the tool taught every artifact shape -- the same maintenance burden as the guards
it backstops, and the pattern-narrower-than-concept failure recurred five times
inside the tool built to catch it. The durable half is the convention, not the
lint: make per-unit rows a required field for any comparative claim. A claim whose
evidence is written down can be checked in seconds; one whose evidence was never
recorded cannot be checked by any tool, and 57 of 60 recent artifacts are in that
category.

